WEBVTT

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.630
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:15.920
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.480
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.730
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.330
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:39.640
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.920
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.050
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.920
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:54.900
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.670
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:03.100
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:06.610
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.840
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:14.040
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.640
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.880
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.260
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.920
<i>Now then, we will</i>
<i>begin this inquiry...</i>

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.490
<i>...into the conduct</i>
<i>of Ensign Shiro Amada.</i>

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:50.270
<i>You are suspected</i>
<i>of being a spy!</i>

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.370
And you say you did nothing out
there you'd want to hide from me?

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.640
If I hadn't handled the
situation that way...

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.840
...the Apsalus would have fallen
into the Federation's hands.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.250
Besides that, I notice you're
dressing very lady-like today.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:07.390
Um, y-yes. Thank you.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.620
Almost like a girl in love...

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.520
Th- That's really not...

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:26.170
We were doing it to survive.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.870
I was just
cooperating with him!

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.310
There seems to be something
more intimate between you.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:37.520
Some day... We'll meet again.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.110
Eliminated.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:44.690
Even though...

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.030
...we are divided into
"enemy" and "ally"...

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.790
...there are good
people on both sides.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.130
People who can
understand each other!

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.170
And for me, knowing that...

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.760
...amidst the stupidity
of this war...

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.740
...is the one thing
that gives me hope!

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.260
<i>Ensign, may I ask</i>
<i>you one question?</i>

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.740
<i>Feeling as you do, can you</i>
<i>still fire at the enemy?</i>

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.570
I think...

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:45.750
I think...

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.590
I think I still don't know.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.760
<i>This inquiry is concluded.</i>

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:59.960
<i>Ensign Shiro Amada, pending</i>
<i>the decision of this tribunal...</i>

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.200
<i>...you are confined to quarters.</i>
<i>These proceedings are now closed!</i>

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:33.700
Amateurs. Trying to
camouflage themselves? Dell!

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:34.740
<i>Yeah?</i>

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.740
We're going to move into...

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.670
<i>...that village up there</i>
<i>to get some food.</i>

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:41.470
<i>You take the new guy and</i>
<i>swing around from the bridge.</i>

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.440
<i>You understand, Arth?</i>
<i>We're not here to cause trouble.</i>

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:52.420
Quit showing off how smart you
are and get us something to eat!

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:53.990
Commander...

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:58.700
You clear on this?
No killing!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.490
<i>Clear as crystal!</i>

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.100
Have you got it?

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.110
Three cyclops are
coming our way!

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:10.840
One from the river,
the others from the bridge.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.100
Make sure my dad
gets this info!

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.410
Roger!

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.500
Don't trip and fall!

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.550
We know!

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:22.680
<i>If they're just after what they said</i>
<i>they're after, we're all right.</i>

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:26.250
<i>But if they find out</i>
<i>we're in the resistance...</i>

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.280
<i>Your facility is going</i>
<i>to become my new base...</i>

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.040
<i>...as part of our reorganization</i>
<i>since we lost Odessa.</i>

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:49.300
What?!

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:51.570
<i>Don't get mad, Genius.</i>

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.980
<i>After all, war is ultimately</i>
<i>about securing positions.</i>

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.880
<i>That little toy of yours...</i>

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.860
<i>...wasn't going to tip the</i>
<i>balance in any major way.</i>

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.920
<i>The deciding fight's going</i>
<i>to be out in space.</i>

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:06.490
<i>Right now, we have to get every</i>
<i>last one of our soldiers up there.</i>

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.830
<i>And for that, we need</i>
<i>your power source there.</i>

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:12.770
<i>We need the</i> Kergeren.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.000
<i>Try to understand, Ginias.</i>

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:17.100
<i>We're canceling development</i>
<i>of the Apsalus.</i>

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.180
<i>This is how you can</i>
<i>show your faith to Zeon...</i>

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:32.950
You dare tell me what faith
is, you war-mad fool!

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.490
Nuclear weapons.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.320
The Minovsky particle.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.690
Mobile suits.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:45.160
In every age, it is the scientists
who change the face of war.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:47.630
Big Brother?!

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:50.470
Are you still here?

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.880
Leave me alone.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:55.310
But!

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.610
Please... Leave me alone.

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:10.960
Please...

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:29.680
Don't.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:31.040
Not yet.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.840
You can't come into the fields!

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:46.130
First to speak
is the loser, huh?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:51.830
That daughter of mine has the
guts to take on a mobile suit.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:55.370
She'll make a good replacement
for me when I'm gone.

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:59.840
By the way, she has a crush on
that Fed officer, doesn't she?

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.570
Yeah, there's something
between them.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:05.310
You know how kids are.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.610
Ah, really. Those two.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.680
My little girl's
acting like a woman.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.380
Two more coming
in from the east.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:15.620
All right!
Keep an eye on them!

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.790
And don't let 'em notice
this house is our base!

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.740
<i>Why's she wasting so much</i>
<i>time on this two-bit village?!</i>

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.480
I'll help 'em
make up their minds...

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.250
<i>Whoops!</i>

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.160
Arth!

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:58.170
Sorry! We didn't mean
to cause any trouble.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:04.070
We were just hoping you'd
share some food with us.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:07.140
Well, then, keep that
monster of yours back!

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:09.270
You coulda just said
so to start with!

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:13.750
We're on the run.
Trust doesn't come easy.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:17.220
Well, we don't have
much to share...

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.480
WE'VE got the mobile suits.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:21.560
Why are we letting
these guys insult us?

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.730
God, can you believe this rain?!

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:32.740
Hey, Pops! Vodka!
Bring the whole bottle here!

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:36.540
And forget the ice.
I don't like it cold.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:39.540
So, your commander's
a Zeek spy.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.980
Must be tough for the
08th Team right now.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.410
The commander... wouldn't
do something like that.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:49.080
Well, it's gotten
you some free time.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.420
You can enjoy yourselves
all afternoon in the bar.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:52.890
You've got nothing
to complain about.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.890
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Relax, friend.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.900
I'm worn out enough!

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:04.160
Why don't I tell you something
interesting instead?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.570
The village where your
guerrilla buddies are?

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:09.730
The Zeon are attacking it.

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:12.030
Kiki's village?!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.340
Well, did they fight?!
Is Kiki okay?!

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:17.940
I don't know any details.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:21.420
The underground sonar just
told us that they're there.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:25.550
You mean... Why isn't
anyone checking it out?!

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:30.820
I reported it. They'll order
someone out if they need to.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.520
Someone besides YOU GUYS.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:39.670
Thanks for your
valuable information.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.970
Here's a drink
for you, my treat.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:44.840
I'll tell the commander!

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.040
Hey, kid!
You forgot your letter!

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:51.580
It looks like Commander Kojima...

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.780
...doesn't think it's worth
sending anyone out.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.890
He said...

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:58.180
Protecting the guerrillas
wasn't our responsibility.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.880
I figured telling you about it
while you're under confinement...

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.930
...would be tough on you, but...

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.660
But I prefer that to
not knowing about it.

00:11:07.170 --> 00:11:08.660
You understand, don't you?

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.700
You could all be
court-martialed.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.290
Court-martialed?!

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.810
We won't get executed, right?

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.010
We can't just abandon friends.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:23.340
I have to pay them back for those
great sandwiches they brought us.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:27.850
Well, I just want
to go help Kiki!

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:31.980
All right, as your
team leader, I order you!

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.960
08th Team, move out!

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:34.890
Aye, sir!

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.620
Not so fast!

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.690
If you three obey his order...

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:44.740
...the newbie here will
take all the blame.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:46.560
But...

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:48.940
So I suggest you use THIS!

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:51.100
An orders form!

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:53.640
With Kojima's
signature on it?!

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:55.770
I'll let you
have it real cheap!

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:58.140
Let's go!

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.740
Listen, kid!

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:02.550
You can't just keep going
head-on against the world.

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:08.260
There are times you need to use the
back doors to get public support.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.890
I'm sorry, Old Man...

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:13.590
That's a step I'm not
ready to take yet.

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:19.230
Typical newbie.
Put it on my tab.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:22.200
We'll pay you back for this.

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:23.870
We owe you.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:27.340
Nothing but trouble...

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.480
You'll never
be good soldiers.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:52.360
<i>If we're going up</i>
<i>against mobile suits...</i>

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:56.100
<i>...why are we waiting</i>
<i>so far from the village?</i>

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:58.610
Dunno.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:01.310
<i>The commander must have</i>
<i>some kind of plan.</i>

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:06.350
Well, we'll see how clever he is.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:11.720
Karen! Sanders! Do you read me?

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:13.020
<i>Aye, sir!</i>

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:17.050
When I give the signal, start
picking off those mobile suits!

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:20.720
Roger. We'll move into
firing range now.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.930
<i>Negative. I want you to</i>
<i>snipe them from there.</i>

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:28.700
W- Wait a minute! That village
is 10 klicks away from here!

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:31.640
Those things have
thermonuclear reactors!

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:33.540
If our shots are even
two meters off, then!

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:36.370
Karen... Those enemy suits...

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:39.940
...are so deep inside the village
we can't fight them there.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.750
Michel, stop the truck!

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:49.460
<i>At least let us move</i>
<i>in another two klicks.</i>

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:50.460
Forget it!

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:54.320
<i>07th Team spotted the</i>
<i>Zakus from that area.</i>

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:56.490
That doesn't mean their sensors
have the same specs as ours!

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.900
The villagers should be
regarded as their hostages.

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.870
We can't be the ones
who start any battles here.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:11.410
If one of those reactors blow,
friend and foe alike get killed.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:14.880
I know that.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:19.120
<i>If worse comes to worst,</i>
<i>I'll cripple one of them.</i>

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:20.960
<i>You take care of the other two.</i>

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:24.190
<i>Can you do that? You just</i>
<i>have anti-tank weapons.</i>

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.620
Pilots know how pilots fight.

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:33.230
Thanks. Once you
secure the comm line here...

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:35.770
...stand by in the hovertruck.

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:38.340
Commander!

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:40.380
It's about the inquiry...

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:42.670
Look...

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:44.940
This isn't worth
killing yourself over.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:48.880
Please, give the order
you always give.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:50.980
About everyone coming
back in one piece.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:57.090
<i>It's okay. I won't</i>
<i>do anything to you.</i>

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:02.160
This is made from
a Zeon shell casing?

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.060
Can I really keep it?

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:07.240
My thanks for giving
us such good food.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:09.240
<i>Thanks, Mister!</i>

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.040
What an idiot.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:15.340
What's the point, tryin' to
make friends with some kid...

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:17.640
<i>Here's your food!</i>

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:21.580
She's a little young,
but beggars can't be choosers.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.030
<i>Arth! Stop it!</i>

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.330
<i>You wouldn't shoot me.</i>

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:41.900
I'll say you were
killed in action.

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:47.010
All right,
I'll put her down.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:51.280
I'll just take my food, first.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.280
You son of a!

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.080
- Miss Kiki!
- No, don't!

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:04.120
We can't risk turning the village
into a battlefield just for revenge!

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:06.760
Wait for our chance!

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:09.660
Serves her right!

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:14.130
You're dead.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.640
It's begun!

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:24.940
Dammit!

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:29.490
Is this maximum
magnification? God dammit...

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:37.420
That idiot!
It was too soon!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.620
Now we can't
let the others go!

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:45.770
They're guerrillas!

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:50.000
Oh, we picked a fine place
to stop for a meal!

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:53.340
<i>Dell! No point staying now!</i>
<i>Let's get out of here!</i>

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:55.610
<i>Roger! Is Arth?</i>

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:59.110
<i>Forget him! I'll cover you!</i>
<i>Can you jump?</i>

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.540
<i>Yeah! I should be</i>
<i>able to manage one!</i>

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:06.350
You're not gettin' away!

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:07.250
Behind me?!

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:26.540
Dammit! They're not
gonna let us escape!

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:29.800
Are you okay?!

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:33.250
Shiro... You're alive...

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:37.080
Where am I?!

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:40.510
In danger. Can you move?

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.920
You... You came to save me?

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:51.870
I came... because this is the
only way I can answer you.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.770
Well, fine!

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:05.310
The cyclops?!
What happened?!

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:07.610
The house...

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:12.480
Dad... Daddy!!!

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:21.260
What's wrong with them?!

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:24.820
If they don't let us go, their
village'll become a battlefield!

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.270
You're not getting away!

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:30.010
Get the women and children
out of the village!

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:33.040
Anyone who can fight,
drive them towards the river!

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:35.770
The river?! Do you WANT
them to get away?!

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.480
At this rate,
the village'll be destroyed!

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:42.580
It doesn't matter, as long
as we pay them back!

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:45.590
Those enemy pilots are
desperate to stay alive, too!

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:48.350
What the hell does a Fed
newbie know about this?!

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:50.830
We won't stop till
they're all dead!

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.760
Kiki, do you feel
the same way?

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.660
I want to make them
pay for my dad!

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:03.230
Yeah! Fight them!
Kill 'em all! Smash the enemy!

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.640
Look, maybe this is
"youthful idealism"...

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:11.440
...but I want to save those
guys in the Zakus, too!

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:18.140
What the hell is
he babbling about?

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:19.650
Shiro...

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:24.320
<i>Karen! Sanders!</i>
<i>Stand by with the beam rifles!</i>

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:04.460
FIRE!!!

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:09.840
<i>Commander!</i>

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.770
Beam weaponry?!

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:21.320
<i>Sanders, correct 0.2</i>
<i>degrees to the left!</i>

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.990
There's no reason
to fight anymore!

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:42.160
<i>Surrender! We'll let you live!</i>

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:46.710
They got Dell, too?

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:48.670
Those idiot guerrillas!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:06.720
Surrender!

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:17.630
Stop it! Don't!

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.510
Anti-personnel weapons!

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:26.550
Get back!

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.890
That's enough!

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:39.960
I'll finish you!

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:42.730
STOP THIS, PLEASE!!!

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:47.900
<i>Can you still</i>
<i>fire at the enemy?</i>

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:06.950
I couldn't do anything.
I couldn't save the villagers.

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:10.820
I couldn't even
prove my own words.

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:19.200
That's not true!
If you hadn't come...

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:21.290
...they would have
wiped us all out!

00:22:21.910 --> 00:22:22.890
Kiki...

00:22:23.010 --> 00:22:24.700
Get away from me!

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:27.440
If you try being nice
to me now, I'll just!

00:22:29.310 --> 00:22:30.640
Thank you...

00:22:51.440 --> 00:22:54.180
osanaikoro kara
All that time that's passed me by.

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:57.870
sou kyou made no so many days
From childhood till now, so many days.

00:22:57.950 --> 00:23:02.010
furikaereba ironna
When I look back, I see so many things...

00:23:02.090 --> 00:23:05.780
koto ni meguriatta
...that happened to come into my life.

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:08.950
naitari warattari
The times I cried, the times I laughed.

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:12.960
kenka shitari yume mitari
The times I fought, the times I dreamed.

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:17.090
chotto hard na shitsuren mo
The lost loves that were sort of hard.

00:23:17.170 --> 00:23:20.230
kagayaku my history
All shining in my history.

00:23:20.910 --> 00:23:23.370
ikutsumono
The ones who caused me pain...

00:23:23.440 --> 00:23:28.240
deai to wakare kugurinukete
...I met and left along the way.

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:34.110
ai suru anata ni sou yo
But I still ended up meeting you.

00:23:34.190 --> 00:23:38.450
Love! meguriaeta
The one that I love.

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:43.350
Ten years after juunen go no
Ten years after, A decade from now.

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:47.120
watashi wa doushiteru darou
I wonder what I will be doing then.

00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:54.260
donna fuu ni anata o sukideiru darou
I wonder how I will be still loving you.

00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:58.370
Ten years after, juunen go no
Ten years after, a decade from now.

00:23:58.440 --> 00:24:02.440
anata o mitsumete mitai
I still want to be looking at you.

00:24:02.510 --> 00:24:06.180
Stay together sono toki
Stay together. When that day comes...

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:12.870
kitto soba de hohoendeitai
...I want to be at your side with a smile.

00:24:16.570 --> 00:24:18.900
Eledore has recovered
and rejoined the 08th Team...

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:20.870
...and now our new orders are...

00:24:20.970 --> 00:24:23.660
...to attack an enemy base
in an airdrop operation!

00:24:24.100 --> 00:24:26.280
Karen's nervous about
making her first drop...

00:24:26.460 --> 00:24:28.560
...and there's something
strange about Sanders.

00:24:29.240 --> 00:24:32.340
And me? I'm still confused...

00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:36.860
But naive thinking like that is just
going to get my team in trouble!

00:24:37.500 --> 00:24:41.820
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam -
The 08th MS Team:

00:24:42.110 --> 00:24:43.320
"Front Line."
